ref:1428a6063b00606e76583315b05c565a7285144a

[local_executor] `Exec` and `ExecRange` explicitly accept intrusive pointer to `ILocallyExecutable`
It will increase number of atomic increments only in one case, when invoking `ExecRange`, and even in this case it will only add one atomic increment.

But this will allow to use fabrics, e.g.:
```
TIntrusivePtr<ILocallyExecutable> MakeExec(...);

TLocalExecutor e;
e.Exec(MakeExec(...), ...);
```

While without this change we will need to write it in the following manner:
```
TIntrusivePtr<ILocallyExecutable> MakeExec(...);

TLocalExecutor e;
{
const auto task = MakeExec(...);
e.Exec(task.Get(), ...);
}
```

We can't write it like `e.Exec(MakeExec(...).Get(), ...)` because after `Get` returns temprary object created by `MakeExec` will be deleted (because ref count will be zero) and it will result in use-after-free.

