Enable CurrentThreadName() on newer Windows and fix tests

* try to load thread name functions from kernel32.dll, if available (Windows version check would not help here, because windows version is mangled if the SDK version used to build the program is a bit old);
* define that TThread::CurrentThreadName() returns empty string on platforms where its functionality is not yet available;
* introduce TThread::CanGetCurrentThreadName() function that reports the usability of CurrentThreadName() and use it in thread-name-related unit tests;

