commit_hash:299f849c2d3cc640866eee3ff82be37f624ac70d

Implement more fine-grained control of specifying links to follow when creating queries.

Instead of something like `follow_links=1`, which would follow all links from the object, the specific links to follow must be named, e.g.:
```
follow_links = {
    "versions": {},
    "developers": {
        "affiliation": {
            "member_of": {}
        }
    },
    "abstraction_level": {}
},
```

The plan is in future to also allow an alternate, easier-to-write representation like:
```
follow_links=["versions", "developers/affiliation/member_of", "abstraction_level"]
```

Extended DataReader to fetch Dividends and Stock Splits from Yahoo!

 - Added yahoo-actions data_source to DataReader;
 - Added get_data_yahoo_actions that returns a DataFrame containing
   DIVIDEND and SPLIT corporate actions fetched from Yahoo! Finance;
 - Added unit tests;
 - Added documentation example.

Implement Nemesis defense

Full implementation of the Nemesis defense:
- Padding on IRQ;
- Storing and clearing all registers on IRQ;
- Restoring registers on RETI;
- Padding on RETI.
